{
 "_readme": "Older salinity seasons (1999-2016) of three KTTV stations from two open datasets, so the salt window starts in 1999. Trà Vinh and Cầu Quan: Mendeley Data 10.17632/fm996rrfyz.1 (Doan Van Binh et al., CC BY 4.0), the yearly maximum, g/l read as ‰ (house convention), no month, so a season counts toward the level and never toward salt months. Mendeley's station named 'Trà Vinh' is ASSUMED to be KTTV's 'Trà Vinh' (unconfirmed). Sơn Đốc: GFZ 10.5880/GFZ.4.4.2024.004 (Apel et al., data from SRHMC, CC BY 4.0), the highest 2-hourly reading of each Oct-Jun season and its month (GFZ's site is 3.5 km from KTTV's approximate Sơn Đốc position); partial = no reading in February or none in March. Coverage is patchy, so a maximum can understate the season. In the Mendeley sheet itself, 1999 and 2000 are identical at the two stations (the other years differ): kept as published, possibly a fill. Where a KTTV bulletin season covers the same station and year, the KTTV value wins (none before 2024).",
